4. The following persons are debarred from being appointed as workmen:-
(i)
Persons below 18 years of age;
(ii)
Persons convicted of offences under the Excise or Opium Act;
(iii)
Persons whose licences have been cancelled under the Excise or Opium Act;
(iv)
Persons of notoriously bad character;
(v)
Persons suffering from an infectious or contagious disease.
